{
  "about": "Pairs measured by tools/contrast.mjs. 'text' needs 4.5:1 (WCAG 2.2 SC 1.4.3, normal-size text); 'non-text' needs 3:1 (SC 1.4.11: component boundaries, focus indicators and graphics needed to understand content). A translucent background (glass) names the backdrops it is measured over in 'over': the world's darkest ground and the brightest light anything in the world reaches. A foreground the world draws translucent names its strength in 'alpha' (a number or an opacity token) and is measured as drawn. One recorded exception: while the calm support panel shows, the world is a dimmed, still backdrop and its trails may fall below 3:1 (every name and state stays in the list beside it); nothing else is exempt. Every pairing a component uses must appear here.",
  "pairs": [
    {"fg": "--text-on-space", "bg": "--surface-space", "kind": "text", "use": "primary text straight on the world's ground"},
